# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Lumen — Git attributes
#
#  Binary policy: store binaries directly in Git, without Git LFS.
#  Rationale: tracked binaries total roughly 22 MB and no single file
#  exceeds 5 MB, which sits comfortably inside GitHub's limits. Avoiding
#  LFS also means a fresh clone gets the images and the model immediately,
#  with no git-lfs install step.
#
#  Historical note: this repository once carried LFS pointer text for the
#  src-tauri/icons files with no matching `filter=lfs` rule, so every
#  clone received broken icons. The 47 images in guide-assets were equally
#  at risk of being replaced by pointer text on `git add`. Both problems
#  are fixed by storing the real bytes. Do not add `filter=lfs` here unless
#  you actually move the assets into LFS and commit the rules in the same
#  commit, so the pointers and the filter can never drift apart.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Auto-detection + normalize line endings to LF ──
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Explicit text files ──
*.ts    text
*.tsx   text
*.js    text
*.jsx   text
*.mjs   text
*.cjs   text
*.json  text
*.md    text
*.html  text
*.css   text
*.py    text
*.rs    text
*.toml  text
*.yaml  text
*.yml   text
*.ini   text
*.cfg   text
*.txt   text
*.sql   text
*.sh    text
*.ps1   text
*.svg   text

# ── Images ──
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.bmp   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.tif   binary
*.avif  binary

# ── Models and binary data ──
*.onnx        binary
*.bin         binary
*.pt          binary
*.pth         binary
*.safetensors binary
*.pkl         binary
*.pickle      binary
*.npy         binary
*.npz         binary

# ── Documents and archives ──
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tar   binary
*.7z    binary

# ── Executables and modules ──
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary
*.wasm  binary

# ── Keep GitHub language stats honest ──
# The illustrated guide and the docs are not source code; they should not be
# counted toward the project's language breakdown.
guide-assets/**          linguist-documentation
docs/**                  linguist-documentation
*.pdf                    linguist-documentation
Lumen-User-Guide-AR.html linguist-documentation

# Alembic templates are generated; keep them out of the language stats.
backend/alembic/versions/** linguist-generated